From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000003 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
Date: Fri, 05 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gcode: raw-string the m112 regex (Python 3.12+ DeprecationWarning, 3.14 SyntaxError)

`re.compile('^(?:[nN][0-9]+)?\s*[mM]112(?:\s|$)')` contains a `\s`
escape inside a NON-raw string.  Behaviour by Python version:

  3.6 - 3.11: silently accepted (a non-existent string escape, in a
              bytes/str literal, decays to the literal backslash + 's'
              — which the regex engine then re-interprets as \s, so
              the regex still does what the author intended).
  3.12 - 3.13: SyntaxWarning at module import (deprecated behaviour).
  3.14+: SyntaxError — module fails to import at all.

We ship Python 3.14 (BR 2026.02.2 LTS default).  Klippy v0.11.0 won't
even load `klippy.gcode` without this fix, and klippy.py imports gcode
unconditionally, so the whole stack fails before reaching the config
parser.

Matches upstream master's fix exactly (klippy/gcode.py:432 on master
is `r'^(?:[nN][0-9]+)?\s*[mM]112(?:\s|$)'` — same raw-string prefix).
The other two re.compile() literals in gcode.py
(args_r line 174, extended_r line 241) are already escape-free /
raw-stringed.

Signed-off-by: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
---
 klippy/gcode.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/klippy/gcode.py b/klippy/gcode.py
--- a/klippy/gcode.py
+++ b/klippy/gcode.py
@@ -393,7 +393,7 @@ class GCodeIO:
         self._dump_debug()
         if self.is_fileinput:
             self.printer.request_exit('error_exit')
-    m112_r = re.compile('^(?:[nN][0-9]+)?\s*[mM]112(?:\s|$)')
+    m112_r = re.compile(r'^(?:[nN][0-9]+)?\s*[mM]112(?:\s|$)')
     def _process_data(self, eventtime):
         # Read input, separate by newline, and add to pending_commands
         try:
